WEBVTT

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:09.926
A NETFLIX SERIES

00:00:19.853 --> 00:00:22.564
KOTARO LIVES ALONE

00:01:11.488 --> 00:01:15.617
TAKUYA

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.286
Oh, I forgot my tissues.

00:01:18.369 --> 00:01:19.996
The Super Rio ones.

00:01:20.080 --> 00:01:22.123
Use my Mun Mun Ranger ones.

00:01:22.207 --> 00:01:24.459
And my Hi Kichu ones too.

00:01:24.542 --> 00:01:26.086
Thanks, everyone!

00:01:26.711 --> 00:01:29.047
Sir Takuya, you can use mine too.

00:01:29.130 --> 00:01:31.591
Oh, what tissues do you have?

00:01:32.634 --> 00:01:35.136
Mine are "Soft Moisturizing Tissues."

00:01:36.346 --> 00:01:37.680
Soft?

00:01:37.764 --> 00:01:39.766
Those tissues aren't cute.

00:01:39.849 --> 00:01:40.683
They're plain.

00:01:40.767 --> 00:01:43.728
Why don't your tissues have a mascot?

00:01:45.438 --> 00:01:46.856
What are you going to buy?

00:01:46.940 --> 00:01:48.066
Box tissues.

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:50.026
Oh, it's you, Kotaro.

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.444
Hello.

00:01:51.528 --> 00:01:52.987
Greetings.

00:01:53.071 --> 00:01:57.242
By the way, the tissues you recommended
are now in stock.

00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:58.284
Really?

00:01:58.993 --> 00:02:00.203
Recommended?

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:01.955
NEW ARRIVAL

00:02:02.038 --> 00:02:03.289
SOFT TISSUES 312 YEN

00:02:03.373 --> 00:02:07.043
One box is 312 yen?! That's too much!

00:02:07.127 --> 00:02:08.253
This is it!

00:02:10.588 --> 00:02:13.216
Kotaro, do you know this one?

00:02:13.299 --> 00:02:17.303
Huh? I've never seen that one.

00:02:17.387 --> 00:02:22.767
This one is pricier,
but I like it because it's comfortable.

00:02:22.851 --> 00:02:25.854
Oh, it has lots of quality ingredients.

00:02:25.937 --> 00:02:28.815
He worries about the ingredients…

00:02:28.898 --> 00:02:32.902
These are so fluffy
and amazing for your skin!

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:35.196
Softness is important for tissues.

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:36.656
It must smell great too.

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:37.574
That's right.

00:02:37.657 --> 00:02:39.367
What's with the tissue talk?

00:02:42.537 --> 00:02:46.291
You should have bought
the same tissues as me, Sir Karino.

00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:47.709
This is a good item.

00:02:47.792 --> 00:02:49.043
It's fine.

00:02:49.127 --> 00:02:51.921
I'm fine with my usual cheap five pack.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:56.217
Most of the expensive tissues
are very soft.

00:02:56.301 --> 00:02:58.386
The so-called moisture-rich tissues.

00:02:58.469 --> 00:03:01.764
In moisturizing tissues,
there are lots of absorbing ingredients

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:03.933
like glycerin and sorbitol

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:08.438
that suck up moisture from the air,
which make the tissues good quality.

00:03:08.521 --> 00:03:11.107
As a result, they are sweeter.

00:03:11.191 --> 00:03:12.066
Sweet?

00:03:12.734 --> 00:03:14.068
You mean the scent?

00:03:15.069 --> 00:03:17.614
Actually, the tissues he gave
as a move-in gift

00:03:17.697 --> 00:03:19.073
were on the expensive side…

00:03:20.241 --> 00:03:23.620
A four-year old who's picky about tissues.
What an enigma.

00:03:25.538 --> 00:03:27.081
Here's the next segment,

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:30.293
"Tell me a personal story!"

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:32.545
A personal story?

00:03:33.254 --> 00:03:35.048
Okay,

00:03:35.131 --> 00:03:40.386
when I was little, there was a period
where my parents didn't come home at all.

00:03:40.929 --> 00:03:42.347
Really?

00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:44.515
I had no one to depend on, no money,

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:46.017
nothing to eat…

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:47.352
What did you do?

00:03:47.435 --> 00:03:51.147
Anyways, I ate tissues in the house
to deal with my hunger.

00:03:51.856 --> 00:03:53.066
Tissues?!

00:03:53.149 --> 00:03:56.069
Right. Tissues taste pretty sweet.

00:03:56.152 --> 00:03:57.946
Oh, they're sweet?

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:00.406
They are sweeter.

00:04:05.954 --> 00:04:06.913
About the other day.

00:04:06.996 --> 00:04:07.830
Huh?

00:04:08.456 --> 00:04:09.916
The tissues that you bought,

00:04:10.959 --> 00:04:12.418
did they taste sweet?

00:04:13.086 --> 00:04:15.213
They were probably sweet.

00:04:15.713 --> 00:04:18.341
What I had before was very sweet.

00:04:18.967 --> 00:04:19.968
I see.

00:04:21.177 --> 00:04:23.096
More importantly, look at this.

00:04:23.179 --> 00:04:26.474
These high quality tissues.
They are full of good ingredients.

00:04:27.684 --> 00:04:30.603
In that case, take these cheaper ones
to the cash register.

00:04:32.355 --> 00:04:35.525
You don't need to eat tissues anymore.

00:04:36.276 --> 00:04:38.194
So, they don't need to be sweet, right?

00:04:44.200 --> 00:04:45.034
Right…

00:04:46.953 --> 00:04:48.329
That is true.

00:05:02.302 --> 00:05:04.012
Bon appétit.

00:05:05.346 --> 00:05:06.180
First,

00:05:06.264 --> 00:05:09.142
is Sir Meat and Potatoes well marinated?

00:05:09.225 --> 00:05:12.603
Sir Tamagoyaki is
always beautifully golden.

00:05:12.687 --> 00:05:16.274
Sir Kinpira Gobo
also seems to be quite crunchy.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:22.113
Sir Sweet and Sour Pork,
are you tender enough?

00:05:25.742 --> 00:05:27.327
What is it, Sir Karino?

00:05:27.410 --> 00:05:29.037
Here, the neighborhood bulletin.

00:05:29.120 --> 00:05:31.122
I see. Thank you very much.

00:05:32.248 --> 00:05:33.124
Oh!

00:05:33.207 --> 00:05:37.003
That is too much food.
And all those small plates.

00:05:37.086 --> 00:05:39.339
I always eat like this.

00:05:39.422 --> 00:05:40.465
Seriously?

00:05:40.548 --> 00:05:41.841
Sorry,

00:05:41.924 --> 00:05:43.926
Kotaro, Karino.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.262
Lady Mizuki, good evening to you.

00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:48.556
I forgot to sign
the neighborhood bulletin.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:51.059
Whoa, amazing!

00:05:51.142 --> 00:05:53.811
- You made all of that?
- Yes.

00:05:53.895 --> 00:05:56.397
Your homemade food!

00:05:56.481 --> 00:05:58.649
- I want to try it.
- Sure.

00:05:58.733 --> 00:06:02.028
What? Really? Hooray!

00:06:02.111 --> 00:06:04.238
Of course
I'll pay full price for the food!

00:06:04.322 --> 00:06:06.657
Well, if Mizuki is coming, I'll come too.

00:06:07.283 --> 00:06:08.451
- Why?
- What?

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:12.538
Either way, that was crazy.

00:06:12.622 --> 00:06:15.708
Having enough dishes to fill that table.

00:06:15.792 --> 00:06:17.543
Yeah, there were a lot, right?

00:06:17.627 --> 00:06:19.420
I'm so excited.

00:06:19.504 --> 00:06:21.631
Why does he have so many dishes?

00:06:21.714 --> 00:06:23.841
It must be a pain to wash all of them.

00:06:23.925 --> 00:06:26.803
He must be particular
about cooking and food, no?

00:06:27.678 --> 00:06:29.222
Particular, right?

00:06:30.848 --> 00:06:33.226
THE DAY OF THE DINNER

00:06:36.979 --> 00:06:38.481
Welcome!

00:06:38.564 --> 00:06:39.524
Yay!

00:06:39.607 --> 00:06:41.192
I've been looking forward to this!

00:06:41.275 --> 00:06:42.693
Let me help with something.

00:06:42.777 --> 00:06:44.654
Thank you for your consideration.

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:48.157
However, since it is almost prepared,
go ahead and relax.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.534
Okay!

00:06:49.617 --> 00:06:53.913
Man, I'm so excited to have the chance
to eat Kotaro's homemade dishes!

00:06:53.996 --> 00:06:54.831
Right?

00:06:54.914 --> 00:06:57.375
What do you think?
Won't there be a lot of dishes?

00:06:57.458 --> 00:07:00.044
Yes, enough for a buffet.

00:07:00.711 --> 00:07:02.588
His dinner table always seems that way.

00:07:02.672 --> 00:07:04.799
Wonder how much food will come out!

00:07:04.882 --> 00:07:07.093
Let's count how many dishes there are!

00:07:08.469 --> 00:07:09.846
Thank you for your patience.

00:07:09.929 --> 00:07:11.305
Whoa!

00:07:12.932 --> 00:07:14.517
Well then, dig in!

00:07:15.726 --> 00:07:16.561
Huh?

00:07:17.145 --> 00:07:18.938
It looks delicious, but…

00:07:19.021 --> 00:07:20.022
one dish?

00:07:20.606 --> 00:07:22.733
What happened here?

00:07:22.817 --> 00:07:25.945
There should be more dishes
after this, right?

00:07:26.028 --> 00:07:27.113
Oh, right.

00:07:27.655 --> 00:07:29.949
I forgot something that I was doing.

00:07:30.032 --> 00:07:32.452
See, there are other dishes.

00:07:33.703 --> 00:07:34.537
Huh?

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:37.373
I also prepared
some background music for today.

00:07:37.457 --> 00:07:38.541
Background music?!

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:41.794
He seems to be welcoming us, but…

00:07:42.378 --> 00:07:46.132
So, is the only dish
this meat and vegetable stir fry?

00:07:46.966 --> 00:07:48.301
Hey, Karino!

00:07:48.384 --> 00:07:51.387
There are some things
you should and shouldn't say, right?

00:07:51.471 --> 00:07:52.555
I mean…

00:07:52.638 --> 00:07:54.307
You're really the worst, Karino!

00:07:54.390 --> 00:07:58.728
Today's meat and vegetable stir fry
came out better than usual!

00:07:59.228 --> 00:08:01.022
Please eat it while it's still hot.

00:08:05.067 --> 00:08:06.235
Thank you for the food!

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:07.403
Please dig in.

00:08:09.572 --> 00:08:11.616
It's so good!

00:08:11.699 --> 00:08:13.951
Well, it's good, but…

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:18.956
This is so good, it's so delicious!

00:08:20.958 --> 00:08:27.924
Yes. I didn't need to make a ton of dishes
as dinner companions today.

00:08:28.424 --> 00:08:30.801
Instead, these people are here.

00:08:31.552 --> 00:08:33.346
Hmm? What's wrong?

00:08:33.429 --> 00:08:35.598
No, I am glad you are all enjoying it.

00:08:35.681 --> 00:08:38.226
I can go for
bowl after bowl of rice with this!

00:08:38.309 --> 00:08:40.394
Right? It's really good!

00:08:40.478 --> 00:08:43.397
I see. Well, would you like another bowl?

00:08:43.481 --> 00:08:44.357
Another bowl!

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.108
- I'll eat it.
- Yes.

00:08:47.693 --> 00:08:49.695
May I have another too?

00:08:52.657 --> 00:08:53.658
A LATER DAY

00:08:53.783 --> 00:08:55.117
Bon appétit.

00:08:56.619 --> 00:08:58.162
Okay, Sir Hijiki.

00:09:00.873 --> 00:09:04.919
ACTOR KOTARO/NIGHT OF A STAR SHOWER

00:09:09.215 --> 00:09:10.758
Okay, time to go.

00:09:13.219 --> 00:09:15.471
This fatigue won't go away.

00:09:15.555 --> 00:09:18.224
My workload's increased,
and there are more things to do.

00:09:20.142 --> 00:09:21.644
No, this face isn't okay!

00:09:24.855 --> 00:09:27.358
I need to smile in front of the kids!

00:09:28.609 --> 00:09:30.444
Smile!

00:09:30.528 --> 00:09:31.654
Okay!

00:09:31.737 --> 00:09:35.741
Then, let's start deciding
our roles for Parents' Day!

00:09:35.825 --> 00:09:36.909
Okay!

00:09:36.993 --> 00:09:40.037
Okay, I'm going to write roles down
on the chalkboard.

00:09:40.788 --> 00:09:43.416
First is Bear!

00:09:43.499 --> 00:09:44.792
Speaking of smiles,

00:09:44.875 --> 00:09:48.754
I realized lately that
since I started teaching this class,

00:09:49.797 --> 00:09:53.593
I haven't seen Kotaro smile even once.

00:09:53.676 --> 00:09:56.178
Is he bored by kindergarten?

00:09:56.262 --> 00:09:58.848
But he sings and dances with everyone,

00:09:58.931 --> 00:10:01.309
and plays with his friends at recess.

00:10:01.392 --> 00:10:02.226
Lady Teacher.

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:05.021
Yes, Kotaro, what is it?

00:10:05.104 --> 00:10:08.190
I would like to be the Smiling Sun.

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:09.191
What?

00:10:09.275 --> 00:10:12.653
Smiling Sun's feature
is that he's always smiling.

00:10:12.737 --> 00:10:14.447
Kotaro wants that role?

00:10:14.989 --> 00:10:18.159
Kotaro, can you really do the Sun?

00:10:18.242 --> 00:10:20.786
I am good at putting on smiles.

00:10:29.962 --> 00:10:31.547
Oh!

00:10:31.631 --> 00:10:35.635
He laughed! It's his smiling face!

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:40.514
Why is he smiling at me?

00:10:41.140 --> 00:10:44.268
You're very good at that, Kotaro.

00:10:44.852 --> 00:10:46.854
What the heck?

00:10:47.855 --> 00:10:50.191
Huh, how is he normally?

00:10:50.274 --> 00:10:53.611
Yes, I wondered what
his usual expressions are like.

00:10:54.111 --> 00:10:57.281
Well, basically,
he always has that same look.

00:10:57.365 --> 00:11:00.451
I've only seen him smile once in passing.

00:11:03.079 --> 00:11:04.872
Is that so?

00:11:04.955 --> 00:11:08.084
To be honest, today we were
deciding roles for Parents' Day

00:11:08.167 --> 00:11:11.003
and Kotaro said he was
"good at putting on smiles"

00:11:11.087 --> 00:11:14.298
and selected a smiling role,
which shocked me.

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:18.886
But, if he's usually like that,
I am a little relieved.

00:11:19.428 --> 00:11:22.390
It's not like
he's not enjoying kindergarten, right?

00:11:22.473 --> 00:11:23.724
I see.

00:11:24.642 --> 00:11:28.020
I can sort of see what he means
by being good at putting on an act.

00:11:28.104 --> 00:11:31.023
When I was in middle school,
I lost my parents

00:11:31.107 --> 00:11:33.067
and went to live with relatives.

00:11:33.651 --> 00:11:35.611
At first, I held back,

00:11:36.362 --> 00:11:39.990
and acted as if the things I disliked
didn't bother me.

00:11:41.033 --> 00:11:43.911
He also seems to have
had a lot happen with his parents.

00:11:43.994 --> 00:11:45.788
He might be reacting like I did.

00:11:46.455 --> 00:11:50.584
I'm wondering if he reads people's faces
and tries to cater to them.

00:11:52.002 --> 00:11:54.255
PARENTS' DAY

00:12:10.646 --> 00:12:13.149
You did well playing the Sun.

00:12:13.232 --> 00:12:14.692
Your smile was wonderful.

00:12:15.276 --> 00:12:17.153
Really? My thanks to you.

00:12:17.236 --> 00:12:22.366
I started thinking that it'd be great
to see your smile with your normal self.

00:12:22.450 --> 00:12:23.534
Yes,

00:12:23.617 --> 00:12:25.953
I can smile well while I'm acting, but…

00:12:27.037 --> 00:12:29.498
Lady Teacher, you're similar to me, right?

00:12:30.332 --> 00:12:32.668
It would be great
if you could smile naturally,

00:12:33.169 --> 00:12:37.715
but it must be hard
to make a smile when you're so tired.

00:12:37.798 --> 00:12:38.632
Why…

00:12:40.634 --> 00:12:43.262
I can see through that.

00:12:47.808 --> 00:12:50.436
I see. So you saw through me?

00:12:51.061 --> 00:12:53.147
Yes. That smile.

00:12:55.649 --> 00:12:58.235
Thank you, Kotaro.

00:13:08.037 --> 00:13:08.954
Newbie,

00:13:09.038 --> 00:13:12.333
we're all going out to eat, so come along.

00:13:12.416 --> 00:13:14.043
It's my treat.

00:13:14.126 --> 00:13:17.087
Sorry, Boss.
I have something to do after this.

00:13:17.671 --> 00:13:18.506
Something to do?

00:13:18.589 --> 00:13:20.883
Yup. I'm gonna climb a mountain.

00:13:21.467 --> 00:13:23.010
Why are you doing that again?

00:13:23.093 --> 00:13:24.512
Did you know, Boss?

00:13:25.179 --> 00:13:28.265
You can see
the Perseids meteor shower today.

00:13:28.349 --> 00:13:30.976
I promised someone
I'd go see it with them.

00:13:31.852 --> 00:13:34.855
Well, I don't know if he remembers.

00:13:41.403 --> 00:13:44.114
Chan

00:13:44.615 --> 00:13:47.827
A new

00:13:47.910 --> 00:13:51.205
dawn has come

00:13:51.288 --> 00:13:53.582
Slash!

00:13:53.666 --> 00:13:55.876
Super strong

00:13:55.960 --> 00:13:58.003
and super kind

00:13:58.087 --> 00:14:01.173
Tonosaman

00:14:02.508 --> 00:14:04.093
It's been a while, Kotaro.

00:14:04.760 --> 00:14:07.638
Yes. It has been a while, Sir Ryota.

00:14:07.721 --> 00:14:10.850
Did you climb up by yourself?
That's dangerous.

00:14:10.933 --> 00:14:12.560
It's nothing.

00:14:12.643 --> 00:14:15.688
Are you by chance
on your way home from work?

00:14:15.771 --> 00:14:18.566
Yeah. I'm working as a carpenter now.

00:14:18.649 --> 00:14:20.568
Though I'm still a newbie.

00:14:20.651 --> 00:14:22.778
Also, since I turned 18 this year,

00:14:22.862 --> 00:14:25.698
I've already left that facility.

00:14:28.951 --> 00:14:30.160
Sir Ryota.

00:14:30.244 --> 00:14:35.249
I ran away in a hurry
without saying goodbye that time.

00:14:36.166 --> 00:14:37.501
I am sorry about that.

00:14:38.085 --> 00:14:39.920
Especially to you and Sir Tasuku--

00:14:40.004 --> 00:14:41.130
I heard later that

00:14:41.672 --> 00:14:45.968
your dad found out you were
in the facility, and it was bad, right?

00:14:46.594 --> 00:14:47.970
So don't worry about it.

00:14:50.681 --> 00:14:54.435
Besides, you remembered our promise.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:56.020
I forgive you.

00:14:57.730 --> 00:14:59.857
Do you like stars, Sir Ryota?

00:15:01.400 --> 00:15:04.320
Yeah. I like seeing them
and taking pictures of them.

00:15:04.403 --> 00:15:06.989
Look. These are photos
I've taken on my camera.

00:15:10.910 --> 00:15:14.288
How amazing. I also like stars.

00:15:14.371 --> 00:15:16.707
It's Tonosaman's trademark!

00:15:16.790 --> 00:15:19.501
Tonosaman? Well, whatever.

00:15:19.585 --> 00:15:22.421
You wanna come with me
when I take pictures of stars?

00:15:23.213 --> 00:15:24.048
Yes!

00:15:24.131 --> 00:15:26.634
Alright, I'll teach you
how to use a camera.

00:15:30.596 --> 00:15:33.390
It's full of photos of stars and you.

00:15:33.474 --> 00:15:36.727
We took a lot.
I'll show them to Tasuku later, too.

00:15:36.810 --> 00:15:37.978
Yes.

00:15:38.062 --> 00:15:39.438
Well then.

00:15:39.521 --> 00:15:42.483
If I don't go back soon,
people will notice I ditched.

00:15:44.193 --> 00:15:45.778
Kotaro, did you know?

00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:50.491
We'll be able to see the Perseids
meteor shower very clearly next summer.

00:15:50.991 --> 00:15:52.368
Is that so?

00:15:52.451 --> 00:15:55.788
On that day, I'd like to see that
on this mountain again.

00:15:56.455 --> 00:15:57.957
Come see that with me.

00:15:59.667 --> 00:16:00.501
Yes!

00:16:02.628 --> 00:16:04.046
I promise!

00:16:05.923 --> 00:16:07.007
Sir Ryota.

00:16:07.925 --> 00:16:11.470
There's one more thing
I want to apologize for.

00:16:13.263 --> 00:16:15.057
Your camera,

00:16:15.140 --> 00:16:18.268
I ended up taking it
when I left the facility.

00:16:19.269 --> 00:16:22.356
I just really wanted to take it with me.

00:16:23.524 --> 00:16:24.608
I am really sorry.

00:16:32.491 --> 00:16:36.954
You and I both took
so many different pictures.

00:16:38.622 --> 00:16:42.084
So, I'll give you my memory card.

00:16:42.668 --> 00:16:45.754
What you really wanted to take,

00:16:45.838 --> 00:16:48.632
were the memories
of the facility on the card,

00:16:48.716 --> 00:16:51.135
rather than the camera, right?

00:16:54.513 --> 00:16:55.889
Thank you!

00:16:56.724 --> 00:16:58.517
Oh, look, Kotaro!

00:16:59.018 --> 00:17:00.853
They're shooting stars!

00:17:03.480 --> 00:17:05.232
Yes! They're beautiful.

00:17:06.942 --> 00:17:11.405
I'm glad I came and got to see
so many shooting stars!

00:17:11.488 --> 00:17:12.698
I am as well!

00:17:22.958 --> 00:17:24.835
SHOGAKUSHA

00:17:25.586 --> 00:17:29.506
BUT IT'S SUNDAY…/THAT BELLY!

00:17:29.590 --> 00:17:33.427
Sir Fukuno.
I brought Sir Karino's manuscript.

00:17:34.011 --> 00:17:34.845
Why?

00:17:35.471 --> 00:17:36.722
Where is Karino?

00:17:36.805 --> 00:17:40.559
Sir Karino has fallen in the hallway
due to a cold.

00:17:40.642 --> 00:17:44.730
My manuscript. I need to take it to…

00:17:47.441 --> 00:17:50.736
Since he was going in and out
of consciousness, I put him on his futon,

00:17:50.819 --> 00:17:52.446
and have come in his place.

00:17:52.529 --> 00:17:54.698
I would have come to get it if he told me.

00:17:54.782 --> 00:17:57.034
Good job coming here on your own.

00:17:57.117 --> 00:17:58.577
Wasn't it dangerous for you?

00:17:58.660 --> 00:18:02.289
What? It's not more dangerous
than Karino in that state.

00:18:02.372 --> 00:18:03.749
Haha.

00:18:03.832 --> 00:18:09.421
Anyway, do you need money that badly,
coming into work on a Sunday?

00:18:09.505 --> 00:18:11.548
Haha. You're mistaken.

00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:14.843
I just have work I need to finish
by the end of the day.

00:18:14.927 --> 00:18:17.304
I come in on weekends every now and then.

00:18:17.805 --> 00:18:20.307
I see, so you are busy.

00:18:20.390 --> 00:18:23.435
Your face always seems glazed over.

00:18:23.519 --> 00:18:25.187
You must be tired.

00:18:25.270 --> 00:18:26.396
Haha.

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.607
Are you eating properly?

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:31.151
Eating is most important when you're busy.

00:18:31.235 --> 00:18:34.947
Haha. This feels like counseling.

00:18:35.030 --> 00:18:36.448
It's okay.

00:18:36.532 --> 00:18:39.034
My wife takes care of me in that regard.

00:18:39.118 --> 00:18:39.993
Huh?

00:18:40.077 --> 00:18:40.994
Huh?

00:18:41.078 --> 00:18:42.913
You were able to get married?

00:18:43.539 --> 00:18:47.209
Haha. What do you mean?

00:18:47.292 --> 00:18:50.712
Well, you are quite skilled
at your job, after all.

00:18:50.796 --> 00:18:52.506
"After all"?

00:18:53.215 --> 00:18:55.342
By the way, I have kids too.

00:18:57.469 --> 00:18:59.096
You should go home right now!

00:18:59.179 --> 00:19:03.517
Your kids must be lonely
when you're working on a Sunday.

00:19:03.600 --> 00:19:05.352
Okay, you should go!

00:19:06.854 --> 00:19:09.940
Haha. You're hitting a sore spot.

00:19:12.276 --> 00:19:14.319
Want to take a field trip?

00:19:14.403 --> 00:19:15.237
Huh?

00:19:15.320 --> 00:19:18.574
We have an editing department
for a kids' toy magazine.

00:19:18.657 --> 00:19:20.826
There are some pretty interesting items.

00:19:20.909 --> 00:19:23.036
I do not require a field trip.

00:19:23.120 --> 00:19:25.664
I believe there's also
some Tonosaman merchandise.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:29.209
It can't be helped.

00:19:29.293 --> 00:19:32.921
If you allow me to view just that,
I'll leave shortly thereafter.

00:19:33.005 --> 00:19:34.256
Haha.

00:19:40.429 --> 00:19:44.141
Well, Sir Fukuno,
you must be satisfied showing me this.

00:19:44.224 --> 00:19:45.893
Hurry up and go home now.

00:19:45.976 --> 00:19:48.353
Haha. He can't take his eyes off this.

00:19:48.437 --> 00:19:50.856
There's also
a big game machine over there.

00:19:51.773 --> 00:19:53.901
I don't need video games. I'm going home.

00:19:59.948 --> 00:20:01.074
Do you like it?

00:20:01.158 --> 00:20:05.078
Don't misunderstand me. I am just
checking the condition of the machine.

00:20:05.162 --> 00:20:06.163
Haha.

00:20:06.914 --> 00:20:11.168
Speaking of which, I believe
we have a two meter tall Tonosaman doll.

00:20:16.173 --> 00:20:19.593
This is the Happy Dance Tonosaman
that was on display

00:20:19.676 --> 00:20:21.303
at the anime anniversary event!

00:20:21.386 --> 00:20:23.263
It's my first time seeing it in person!

00:20:23.347 --> 00:20:24.890
It is amazing!

00:20:28.268 --> 00:20:31.438
Sir Fukuno,
you should not be entertaining me.

00:20:32.147 --> 00:20:35.651
Isn't this a disservice to your children?

00:20:35.734 --> 00:20:38.862
Hmm. He's a tough nut to crack.

00:20:40.405 --> 00:20:42.783
I truly apologize about Sunday.

00:20:42.866 --> 00:20:45.702
When I woke up, I was on my futon.

00:20:45.786 --> 00:20:46.787
Haha.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:49.623
Kotaro came by himself
with the manuscript.

00:20:50.207 --> 00:20:53.794
He said that
he got to see the editing department,

00:20:53.877 --> 00:20:56.255
but he seemed down for some reason.

00:20:56.338 --> 00:20:58.924
I wonder if I ended up
hurting him after all.

00:20:59.007 --> 00:20:59.841
What is it?

00:21:00.425 --> 00:21:03.345
I have a wife and kids…

00:21:03.428 --> 00:21:04.972
What?!

00:21:05.055 --> 00:21:07.808
You're overdoing it. Well, whatever.

00:21:08.392 --> 00:21:11.561
I feel this more
because I see my own kids,

00:21:11.645 --> 00:21:14.273
but Kotaro acts, how should I say this,

00:21:14.356 --> 00:21:16.316
strangely mature for his age.

00:21:17.651 --> 00:21:19.611
So I wanted him to get more excited,

00:21:19.695 --> 00:21:21.321
enjoy himself, laugh…

00:21:23.115 --> 00:21:26.034
I wanted to see Kotaro act that way.

00:21:26.994 --> 00:21:32.416
I want Kotaro to enjoy being a child,
just a little bit more.

00:21:35.002 --> 00:21:37.004
All right, your deadline is next week.

00:21:37.087 --> 00:21:37.921
Got it.

00:21:40.299 --> 00:21:41.508
Sir Fukuno.

00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:45.637
Kotaro, what's going on?

00:21:47.347 --> 00:21:50.726
I can go on another field trip,
if it's on a weekday.

00:21:53.770 --> 00:21:54.938
Haha.

00:22:04.990 --> 00:22:07.200
Oh, Kotaro, it's been a while!

00:22:07.284 --> 00:22:09.119
Today's free samples are wieners.

00:22:09.202 --> 00:22:10.245
Would you like one?

00:22:11.705 --> 00:22:14.082
SHIMIZU WIENERS MADE IN JAPAN
135 YEN

00:22:14.166 --> 00:22:17.336
- I will buy all of those wieners.
- What?!

00:22:19.379 --> 00:22:20.589
What, seriously?!

00:22:21.340 --> 00:22:22.883
NEXT DAY
CORN POTATO SOUP DAY

00:22:22.966 --> 00:22:24.801
THE DAY AFTER THAT
DANISH PASTRY DAY

00:22:24.885 --> 00:22:27.054
You've been generous lately.

00:22:29.806 --> 00:22:31.141
Miss Food Sample Lady!

00:22:31.224 --> 00:22:33.769
Hmm? Kotaro?
Did you forget to buy something?

00:22:33.852 --> 00:22:35.520
I was worried.

00:22:35.604 --> 00:22:38.523
- Hmm?
- About your stomach.

00:22:38.607 --> 00:22:40.108
Oh, this is…

00:22:40.192 --> 00:22:45.989
In your work, do you need to clean up
everything if there are leftovers?

00:22:46.073 --> 00:22:47.157
Hmm?

00:22:47.240 --> 00:22:51.119
Before I realized it, you had gained
a fair amount of weight.

00:22:55.457 --> 00:22:56.416
A baby?

00:22:57.167 --> 00:22:58.460
That's right!

00:22:58.543 --> 00:23:02.214
I'm not being forced to eat
what I don't sell, so don't worry!

00:23:02.297 --> 00:23:05.217
That's why you've been
buying in bulk lately!

00:23:05.300 --> 00:23:08.678
Yes. Are you making fun of me?

00:23:08.762 --> 00:23:10.639
I'm telling you, it's true!

00:23:10.722 --> 00:23:13.308
This stomach, it is not a peach, right?

00:23:13.392 --> 00:23:16.770
CRACKS OPEN SPLASH HEAVE, HO!

00:23:18.021 --> 00:23:20.399
Aren't you talking about
the Momotaro folktale?

00:23:21.691 --> 00:23:24.986
Hey, you should not laugh at folktales.
They are good.

00:23:25.737 --> 00:23:29.241
Momotaro is special, but really,

00:23:29.324 --> 00:23:31.743
babies are made with love.

00:23:31.827 --> 00:23:35.247
When a father and mother love each other,

00:23:35.747 --> 00:23:38.250
they can make a baby
in the mother's belly.

00:23:40.335 --> 00:23:42.170
Is this true for me as well?

00:23:42.254 --> 00:23:43.463
Of course!

00:23:43.547 --> 00:23:46.383
You were born from
the love of your mom and dad!

00:23:46.466 --> 00:23:47.342
Kotaro!

00:23:47.843 --> 00:23:49.553
I see!

00:23:53.932 --> 00:23:58.770
This child is a treasure that will make
his father and myself happy!

00:24:02.023 --> 00:24:04.192
Treasure.

00:24:12.242 --> 00:24:14.828
You were born from
the love of your mom and dad!

00:24:14.911 --> 00:24:15.745
Kotaro!

00:24:16.246 --> 00:24:21.209
This child is a treasure that will make
his father and myself happy!

00:24:21.835 --> 00:24:27.841
Sir Hanbe, do you have memories of
your father and mother loving each other?

00:24:29.050 --> 00:24:30.677
I don't have any.

00:24:31.887 --> 00:24:36.391
If the treasure's role
is to make their parents happy,

00:24:37.058 --> 00:24:41.605
I wonder if I'm fulfilling that role
even a little bit.

00:24:45.734 --> 00:24:49.237
Lady Kobayashi, thank you for
giving me the living expenses every week.

00:24:49.321 --> 00:24:50.780
No, it's no problem!

00:24:50.864 --> 00:24:52.073
Here you are.

00:24:52.157 --> 00:24:53.909
Thank you always for your kindness!

00:24:56.578 --> 00:24:57.954
Yokan and,

00:24:58.622 --> 00:25:02.626
the usual week's worth of
seven diary entries to the kind person.

00:25:09.841 --> 00:25:11.927
Huh? There's an eighth page?

00:25:12.928 --> 00:25:15.138
"I will do my best to be a treasure"?

00:25:15.764 --> 00:25:17.015
What does this mean?
